    "updated_at": "2021-03-17T10:13:28Z",
    "body": "Yup, it is definitely Perl's one-humped camel 🐪 while OCaml uses a two-humped one 🐫. \n\nAlso, the latest version of OCaml as of writing this is [4.12.0](https://ocaml.org/releases/) so you either traveled to the future or that is just good old Perl5. 😀 ",
